<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Heavy rains to halt harvesting.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Heavy rains to halt harvesting.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heavy rains fell overnight across southern Kansas and northern Oklahoma, and grain dealers said the excessive moisture would likely halt harvesting Thursday.</p>
<p>Dealers said Dodge City, in southwest Kansas, got around 3-1/2 inches of rain. Garden City, Kan., was hit with about 2-1/2 inches.</p>
<p>&quot;We were hoping that farmers would start cutting today but with this happening it's going to delay (harvesting) until late Friday and probably Saturday,&quot; a south central Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>Grain dealers said the heavy rains would probably also reduce test weights.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, while yield reports continued to be high, dealers said there were many reports of low protein levels.</p>
<p>&quot;Yields are fine, but the problem seems to be low protein -- like down near nine percent on a lot of fields,&quot; an Oklahoma dealer said. &quot;Southeast Kansas in particular has an abundance of low protein fields.&quot;  </p>
